          "title": "You'll want to know: മാൾ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മാൾ — māḷ — \"a shopping mall\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഞായറാഴ്ച മാളിൽ വലിയ തിരക്കായിരുന്നു. ñāyaṟāḻca māḷil valiya tirakkāyirunnu. The mall was very crowded on Sunday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A loan ending in a chillu: മാൾ (māḷ), മാളിൽ, in the mall."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മാൾ (māḷ) was borrowed from English mall, a large building full of shops."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
